    {
      "key": "logistics",
      "title": {
        "en": "Initial Logistical Engagement Considerations"
      },
      "description": {
        "en": "Conditionalities / leading questions to cause further thinking and dialogue on operationalisation This is NOT an approach to generate an answer. It is to structure questioning and how we think about how we are to work. The practicality of initial engagement to develop the foundations for further, more engaged work. The higher the score, the greater the flexibility in our direct engagement. However, where we can sense potential, then we look at how we develop our own expectations and working styles to be to deliver outputs (set to context) and build for next level engagement. Under State auspices, we seek district-to-district engagement. Given political decisions on priority districts, this initial thinking is open to development and can be used as basis for taking forward institutional development at all governmental levels. It can be the basis for how different elements in government interact to assess and address key areas of policy (into practice). All FMSs have Articles or Laws noting the critical role of the district, even sub-district, in government, governance. However, the practicality of governance is not keeping pace with consultants writing laws and policies. Credibility of government will be a critical element in what we do to reinforce democratization. The development of what a social contract should have in it and what it means in tangible terms will involve how we work with and through government at state, district and gain feedback from sub-district) levels. Key elements beyond the council formation and the induction of councillors will be how State is to support delivery of the district and state government. How peace dividend is realised through technocractic approaches noting resourcing, technical people, skills as well as funds, is going to be critical."
      },
